  "description": "Faithful replication with the original videos and scene pictures: each participant is randomly assigned to one of six office spaces that differ only in their wooden furniture, 3 wood colours (light #ECCD97, medium #ECB36C, dark #95582C) x 2 wood coverages (low 12%, high 35%). They watch a 35 s walk-through video of that office, then spend 1 minute imagining themselves working and talking with others there while looking at four pictures of it from different angles, and then rate it: sensory evaluation ('What do you think of the office environment?', 10 adjectives: bright, spacious, organized, relaxing, natural, harmonious, vivid, comfortable, beautiful, attractive), satisfaction (2 items) and usage willingness (2 items), all on 7-point scales. Demographics follow. Rebuilt from Zhu, Wang & Zhao (2022), Wood in office spaces: The impact of different wooden furniture on aesthetic evaluation, Frontiers in Psychology 13: 986627, with its Supplementary Videos 1-6 (rendered in Lumion) and scene pictures (Supplementary Image 1 and Figures 7-11), CC BY 4.0. Media ids: <colour>_<coverage>.mp4 and <colour>_<coverage>_scenes.jpg; 'condition' records the assignment. Analysis as in the paper: 3 x 2 between-subjects ANOVA (or Kruskal-Wallis / Mann-Whitney) on the mean of each scale; the paper found light and medium wood rated above dark and low coverage above high, with medium-low best on sensory evaluation (5.70) and dark-high lowest on all three. Differences from the original study: (1) the paper's opening PANAS mood measure (Qiu et al. 2008 Chinese revision, 18 adjectives, used as a covariate) is left out because its items are not printed in the paper; (2) the scale anchor labels are ours (the paper says only '7-point scale'); English item wording from the paper, which ran in Chinese on questionnaire.com; (3) videos are re-encoded to 960 x 540 to fit the upload limit; (4) the paper's analysed ratings were per-scale means; the platform stores each item; demographic wording is ours, after the paper's participant description.",
  "logoPosition": "right",
